=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The network is fully healthy for PC11. Every layer of the data path was
inspected and tested with live traffic, and no fault was found anywhere.

PC11 (172.16.20.11/24) has its eth0 link in UP/LOWER_UP state with the
correct IP address and no iptables rules. On switch2, port eth5 — the
only physical connection to PC11 — is correctly enslaved to the
br_vlan20 bridge (the VLAN20 access domain), PC11's MAC address is
dynamically learned in the FDB, and no tc filters or port-security rules
are applied. The switch2 startup script confirms the intended
configuration: eth3–eth6 are access ports for VLAN20 and eth0/eth1/eth2
carry VLAN20 traffic upstream via 802.1Q tagged sub-interfaces.

On the multilayer-switch side, mswitch0's vlan20 SVI (172.16.20.254/24)
is up, its ARP table shows 172.16.20.11 → 62:6c:a5:68:c6:4a with state
REACHABLE, and the iptables FORWARD chain and ebtables chains are all
empty with ACCEPT policies.

Live ping tests confirmed zero packet loss: PC11 reaches its on-VLAN
peers (PC9, PC10), the VLAN20 gateway (172.16.20.254), cross-VLAN hosts
(172.16.10.5, 172.16.30.12), and is reachable from outside the VLAN in
the reverse direction. The symptom described in ticket #8129 — that PC11
cannot reach anything, including adjacent machines — is not reproducible
and is not supported by any evidence in the live lab.

Root cause: there is no fault; the ticket describes a condition that does
not exist in the network.

Corrective action: close the ticket as a false alarm. No configuration
changes are required.
=== END ===
